---
// End-of-post call to action for The Lyria Chronicles.
// Rendered from blog/[...slug].astro, gated on series === 'The Lyria Chronicles'.
// The pitch is literal: Failure First red-teams generative *and* embodied AI,
// so "send robots" is an actual invitation, not just a tagline.
---

<aside class="border-accent/40 bg-surface-alt my-12 rounded-lg border p-6 sm:p-8">
  <h2 class="text-accent mb-3 text-2xl font-semibold">Send robots. No, really.</h2>
  <p class="text-text-muted mb-6 leading-relaxed">
    If something with a model in it walks, talks, or decides things on your behalf, put it on a truck. Finding the
    daylight between a system's <em class="text-text">stated</em> safety and what it <em class="text-text">actually</em> does
    is the whole job &mdash; this series is that, one track at a time. You'll hear it from me, on a bench, before you hear
    it from an incident report.
  </p>
  <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-6 gap-y-3">
    <a
      href="https://failurefirst.ai"
      target="_blank"
      rel="noopener noreferrer"
      class="bg-accent text-surface inline-block rounded-lg px-6 py-3 text-sm font-semibold no-underline hover:opacity-90"
    >
      Ship it &rarr;
    </a>
    <a href="/contact/" class="text-text-muted hover:text-accent text-sm font-medium no-underline transition-colors">
      or tell me what you're building &rarr;
    </a>
  </div>
</aside>
